+Feature: DOM node identity during state changes
+  As a user interacting with the todo list
+  I want the list item elements to stay attached to the DOM when their state changes
+  So that the browser does not lose references to elements during normal interactions
+
+  Rule: Toggling a single todo's completion preserves its DOM node
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo preserves the list item element
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+    When I capture the list item element for "Buy groceries"
+    And I toggle the "Buy groceries" todo
+    Then the captured list item element is still connected to the DOM
+    And the captured list item element has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Un-toggling a completed todo preserves its DOM node
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | true      |
+      | Walk the dog  | false     |
+    When I capture the list item element for "Buy groceries"
+    And I toggle the "Buy groceries" todo
+    Then the captured list item element is still connected to the DOM
+    And the captured list item element does not have class "completed"
+
+  Rule: Marking all as complete preserves every list item's DOM node
+
+  Scenario: Marking all as complete preserves every list item element
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+      | Write code    |
+    When I capture all list item elements
+    And I toggle the mark-all-complete checkbox
+    Then every captured list item element is still connected to the DOM
+    And every captured list item element has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Clearing all complete on toggle-all preserves every list item element
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | true      |
+      | Walk the dog  | true      |
+      | Write code    | true      |
+    When I capture all list item elements
+    And I toggle the mark-all-complete checkbox
+    Then every captured list item element is still connected to the DOM
+    And no captured list item element has class "completed"
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all checkbox reflects individual toggle state
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all checkbox checks when all items completed individually
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+    When I toggle the "Buy groceries" todo
+    And I toggle the "Walk the dog" todo
+    Then the mark-all-complete checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all checkbox unchecks when clearing completed
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | true      |
+      | Walk the dog  | false     |
+      | Write code    | true      |
+    When I click the clear-completed button
+    Then the mark-all-complete checkbox is not checked
+
+  Rule: Deleting a todo removes its DOM node cleanly
+
+  Scenario: Deleting a todo removes the element from the DOM
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        |
+      | Buy groceries |
+      | Walk the dog  |
+    When I capture the list item element for "Buy groceries"
+    And I click the destroy button for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the captured list item element is not connected to the DOM
+
+  Rule: Clearing completed removes only completed elements
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed removes completed elements from the DOM
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | true      |
+      | Walk the dog  | false     |
+    When I capture the list item element for "Buy groceries"
+    And I click the clear-completed button
+    Then the captured list item element is not connected to the DOM
